{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8a3b36d4", "timestamp": "2026-06-12T10:57:00", "text": "Absolutely, we're here to help! Thanks for tackling this, @eid_2604c806. 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260616-10-1c858"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260616-10-1c858"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86044ae5", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:05:00", "text": "Hi team, 👋 I wanted to kick off a discussion about our new UI feature with drag-and-drop functionality. I've found some interesting open-source projects that have implemented similar features. Let's dive in and see what we can learn! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260615-0-79328"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-0-79328"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86044ae5", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:09:00", "text": "First up, we have JupyterLab's 'Interactive Notebook Layout with Drag-and-Drop'. This PR implements a drag-and-drop interface for rearranging cells and components within a notebook. You can check it out here: https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/pull/2350. Thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260615-1-ce402"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-1-ce402"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_dbc6178f", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:13:00", "text": "@George Brown, I think JupyterLab's approach is quite relevant to us. Their focus on rearranging components could be really useful for our forecast models. It seems like a smooth and intuitive experience for users. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260615-2-038da"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-2-038da"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1bf91687", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:16:00", "text": "Agreed, Hannah! JupyterLab's implementation could definitely inspire our layout design. I like how they maintain a clean interface while adding functionality. We should consider how they handle user feedback during the drag-and-drop process. 📊", "utterranceID": "20260615-3-f9ac4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-3-f9ac4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86044ae5", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:21:00", "text": "Great points, @Hannah Garcia and Julia! Next, let's look at WordPress's 'Customizable Page Builder with Drag-and-Drop'. This PR introduces a drag-and-drop page builder for creating and customizing page layouts effortlessly. Here's the link: https://github.com/WordPress/WordPress/pull/2351. What do you think? 🛠️", "utterranceID": "20260615-4-eef49"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-4-eef49"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1bf91687", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:23:00", "text": "WordPress's page builder is quite powerful. It allows users to create complex layouts without any coding. This could be a great reference for making our UI more accessible to non-technical users. We should definitely consider their approach to modular design. 🧩", "utterranceID": "20260615-5-bf153"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-5-bf153"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_dbc6178f", "timestamp": "2026-06-15T20:26:00", "text": "I agree, Julia. The modular design is key. Plus, WordPress's emphasis on customization could help us offer more flexibility in our models. We should look into how they manage component interactions. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260615-6-15a18"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260615-6-15a18"}

