{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:16:00", "text": "Blueprints are a fantastic way to keep things modular. @eid_2347b567, maybe we can adapt this concept to ensure our API remains scalable as it grows. What do you think?", "utterranceID": "20261008-6-2dd15"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-6-2dd15"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:21:00", "text": "Absolutely, Fiona. I'll look into how we can incorporate a similar modular design. It could really help us maintain a clean architecture. 🛠️", "utterranceID": "20261008-7-2fa75"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-7-2fa75"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_54905dcb", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:23:00", "text": "Flask's simplicity is always appealing. Their blueprints could definitely help us avoid a monolithic structure.", "utterranceID": "20261008-8-02424"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-8-02424"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:27:00", "text": "Lastly, we have Express.js's [Middleware for Enhanced API Security](https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/3156). This feature implements middleware for security enhancements like rate limiting and input validation.", "utterranceID": "20261008-9-88c00"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-9-88c00"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df3bcc2", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:28:00", "text": "Security is crucial. Express.js's middleware approach is something we should definitely consider. Rate limiting and input validation are essential for protecting our API.", "utterranceID": "20261008-10-ff2eb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-10-ff2eb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:29:00", "text": "Yes, security can't be an afterthought. We should look into how Express.js structures their middleware and see if we can integrate similar security measures.", "utterranceID": "20261008-11-de4a2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-11-de4a2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T16:33:00", "text": "I'll take a closer look at these features and see how we can adapt them to our needs. Thanks for the input, everyone! Let's keep the ideas flowing. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261008-12-ed1ba"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-12-ed1ba"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T20:38:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for initializing the RESTful API framework: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/5. I've set up the foundational structure, installed essential libraries, and completed the basic server setup to handle HTTP requests. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261012-0-04b1d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261012-0-04b1d"}
